<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yaa Asantewaa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1840–<a href="/years/1921">1921</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yaa Asantewaa was the Queen Mother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ejisu">Ejisu</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Ashanti Empire</a>, who led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-golden-stool">War of the Golden Stool</a> against British rule in 1900. The uprising was provoked by the British governor's demand to sit on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-stool">Golden Stool</a>. After months of resistance she was captured and exiled, and she is remembered as a heroine of anti-colonial resistance in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yaa-asantewaa.jpg" alt="Yaa Asantewaa" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Noahalorwu · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ejisu_Roundabout.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
